    <h1>All About Colors</h1>

    <p>
        Colors are an important part of our everyday life.
        They make things beautiful and help us identify different objects.
    </p>

    <h2>Primary Colors</h2>

    <p>
        The three primary colors are:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Red</li>
        <li>Blue</li>
        <li>Yellow</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Secondary Colors</h2>

    <p>
        Secondary colors are created by mixing two primary colors.
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Red + Yellow = Orange</li>
        <li>Blue + Yellow = Green</li>
        <li>Red + Blue = Purple</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Common Colors and Their Meanings</h2>

    <table border="1">
        <tr>
            <th>Color</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Red</td>
            <td>Love, danger, energy and passion</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Blue</td>
            <td>Peace, trust and calmness</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Green</td>
            <td>Nature, growth and freshness</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Yellow</td>
            <td>Happiness, brightness and optimism</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Purple</td>
            <td>Royalty, creativity and luxury</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Orange</td>
            <td>Energy, excitement and enthusiasm</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Black</td>
            <td>Power, elegance and mystery</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>White</td>
            <td>Peace, purity and simplicity</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h2>Conclusion</h2>

    <p>
        Colors are useful in art, fashion, websites, advertisements,
        decoration and many other areas. Learning about colors can help
        us understand how different colors work together.
    </p>

